    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0168" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg34"/>

                <head>No. 31.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Tree.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 26,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch (No. 289) of the 6th instant,
                    reporting your action under my instruction (No. 90) of the 7th ultimo relative
                    to the alleged <pb facs="0169" n="35" xml:id="pg35"/> wrongs inflicted on the
                    American Baptist Missionary Union by Mr. Henry M. Stanley and the Congo State
                    authorities, has been received.</p>
                <p>Your report of the restitution of the steamer and indemnification of the owners
                    has been read with satisfaction.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
